.TH BTK-NODE 1 "15 August 2026" "Bitcoin Toolkit 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btk-node \- Bitcoin P2P version handshake (IPv4 mainnet)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btk node
.B \-\-host
.I HOST
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fI8333\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to a Bitcoin P2P peer, sends a
.B version
message, prints the peer's
.B version
as a typed object, and closes. Does not send
.BR verack .
IPv4 mainnet only. 15 second timeout. Default port 8333.
.PP
.B \-\-host
is required. A leftover positional is
.BR "provide input on stdin"
(the host is a flag, not an item payload). If
.B \-\-host
contains a single colon, the suffix is the port. Combined with
.B \-\-port
that is
.BR "port specified twice" .
.PP
.B \-\-stream
is an error
.RB ( "node does not stream" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
IPv4 address or DNS name. Required. A
.I host:port
form sets the port.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " 8333"
TCP port. Default 8333.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Include
.B raw
with
.BR addr_recv ,
.BR addr_trans ,
.BR nonce ,
and
.BR services_bits .
.TP
.BI \-\-out " ndjson|json|plain"
Output framing. Default ndjson.
.B \-\-out plain
prints
.IR ip:port .
.SH OUTPUT
The typed object includes
.BR host ,
.BR ip ,
.BR port ,
.BR protocol ,
.BR user_agent ,
.BR height ,
.BR services
(named bits in ascending order; unknown set bits are
.BR BIT_n ),
.BR relay ,
and
.BR timestamp .
.SH NOTES
Does not load
.IR ~/.btk/config.json .
Does not speak IPv6, testnet, or the rest of the peer protocol.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btk (1)
